---
import DcaSimulator from '../components/DcaSimulator.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { btcHistory } from '../lib/data';

const asOf = btcHistory.series.at(-1)?.date;
---

<Base
  title="blockplot · DCA simulator"
  description="Simulate weekly or monthly BTC dollar-cost averaging vs an equal lump sum from any start date, fees included."
>
  <h1 class="visually-hidden">DCA simulator</h1>

  <section class="chart-section">
    <h2>DCA vs lump sum · fully client-side</h2>
    <DcaSimulator />
    <p class="method-note">
      Each scheduled buy spends the fixed amount, less the per-buy fee, at that day's close (a
      schedule date missing from the data buys on the next available day; month-end schedules
      clamp, e.g. Jan 31 → Feb 29; two schedules landing on the same day collapse into one buy,
      shrinking the budget accordingly). The lump sum invests the same total budget on the start
      date with the same fee rate applied once. Undeployed DCA cash counts toward wealth, so both
      strategies start from the same budget and the comparison is like-for-like. Prices are
      blockchain.com daily closes through {asOf}; the simulation runs entirely in
      the browser on the committed dataset with the same fixture-tested functions as the pipeline,
      and ignores taxes, slippage, and yield on idle cash.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
